Description: CVE-2026-50252 - Possible cache poisoning attack by mapping source port population per thread.
 Unbound shared a single population of source ports across all worker
 threads, which reduced the entropy of the (source port, query ID) tuple
 available to an off-path attacker and made cache poisoning attacks more
 feasible. This patch introduces a shared_ports structure that maps the
 source port population per thread, restoring the intended per-thread port
 randomisation. It also folds in the follow-up commits that guard access to
 the shared ports interface array during initialisation/thread setup, fix a
 sign-of-comparison warning, and fix unused-variable warnings when compiled
 without threads.
 .
 Includes the upstream regression test additions in testcode/unittcpreuse.c.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/804cff4c152a121961b04605f75132370fc80df4
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/ca1fe4f82a7c5d8168562edc03abd455950c5dbe
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/e183c2c506efffef7ea28ee7243bf9d8da6bc542
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/8f7411057f655cda8f06bc0fac81a01eed926dd2
Author: W.C.A. Wijngaards <wouter@nlnetlabs.nl>
Last-Update: 2026-07-28
