Description: CVE-2026-55990 - Packet of death for a DNSCrypt misconfigured Unbound
 A misconfigured DNSCrypt-enabled Unbound (a dnscrypt-provider-cert without a
 matching dnscrypt-secret-key) leaves certificate entries with a NULL keypair.
 A crafted DNSCrypt query that matches such a certificate's magic_query causes
 a NULL pointer dereference (denial of service) when the query is decrypted.
 .
 This fix zero-initializes the certs array, skips certificate entries that have
 no keypair in dnsc_find_cert(), and makes dnsc_apply_cfg() fail at startup when
 one or more provider certs have no matching secret key.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/ae1b3810cc3a8eb9b43c378289f74020b42aa7f4
Author: W.C.A. Wijngaards <wouter@nlnetlabs.nl>
Last-Update: 2026-07-28
---
--- a/dnscrypt/dnscrypt.c
+++ b/dnscrypt/dnscrypt.c
