Description: CVE-2026-50045 - 'max-global-quota' reset by DNSSEC validation restarts
 Unbound tracks the number of upstream queries generated while resolving a
 client query against the 'max-global-quota' limit. That per-request global
 quota counter lived only in the iterator's per-query target_count state and
 was lost whenever the module state was torn down and restarted, for example
 when the validator restarts iteration for a DNSSEC lookup (DS/DNSKEY) or when
 a subquery is generated. An attacker could therefore drive an effectively
 unbounded number of upstream queries for a single client request by forcing
 repeated validation restarts, defeating the amplification/loop protection
 the quota is meant to provide.
 .
 This fix persists the reached global quota in the module_qstate
 (global_quota_reached / global_quota_started) so the counter survives module
 restarts: the iterator stores the value on finish/clear and picks it back up
 when the target_count structure is (re)created, and the validator propagates
 the counter into generated subqueries and back up to the super query in
 val_inform_super. target_count_create / _increase / _increase_nx /
 _increase_global_quota gain a module_qstate parameter and a new
 target_count_store helper carries the value across restarts.
